Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients hospitalized in a Psychiatric Inpatient Unit;
* Adults aged 18 years or older;
* SAKp Fall Risk Scale with a moderate risk score (6.5 to 10 points) or high risk (10.5 points or higher);
* Clinical and cognitive conditions that allow the performance of physical exercises;
* Patients with an expected hospital stay of 12 days or longer, in order to ensure minimum exposure to the proposed intervention;
* Agreement to participate in the study by signing the Informed Consent Form.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Age ≥ 40 years;
* Spontaneous intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH) confirmed by neuroimaging;
* Hematoma volume 15-60 mL;
* Within 48 hours of symptom onset (if onset time is unknown, the time last seen normal is used);
* Meeting one of the following: basal ganglia or lobar hemorrhage with NIHSS score ≥ 8; or thalamic, brainstem or cerebellar hemorrhage with Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) score 7-14;
* Written informed consent obtained from the patient or the legal representative.

